   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the central New\nYork regional transportation authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S8439",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8439-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1328, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8439\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the central\nNew York regional transportation authority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo make amendments to the enabling law of the Central NY Regional Trans-\nportation Authority (\"CENTRO\") to update and modernize the board of\ndirectors.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 1328 of the Public Authorities Law to increase\nthe maximum number of the CENTRO Board from 12 to 16 members. It grants\nnew CENTRO member Cortland County 1 seat along with 1 seat each to\ncurrent members Cayuga and Oswego. It guarantees one board seat to the\nremaining counties eligible to become CENTRO members should they wish to\njoin at a later date (Jefferson, Madison). Additionally, it adds\nprovisions to allow current board members to continue to serve past the\nexpiration of their term if the Governor fails to make a re-appointment\nor replacement. Finally, if a vacancy occurs midterm, new language will\nallow if the vacancy is not filled before the term expires, then the new\nappointee can serve a full 7-year term.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCENTRO recently added Cortland County as its 5th member. To account for\nits expansion and the possibility of adding Jefferson and/or Madison\ncounties in the future, CENTRO requested this change in its enabling\nlegislation. Expanding the board from 12 to 16 members provides CENTRO\nwith the necessary room for growth. The bill also removes old language\npreviously attempted to add board seats based on population. Only Onon-\ndaga and Oneida counties currently have populations above 100,000. The\nbill also has new language to deal with vacancies on the board and reap-\npointments that go unfilled by the Governor to ensure a quorum and\ncontinuity on the CENTRO board.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have been\nin full force and effect on and after March 31, 2025.\n",
