    "lawCode": "Amd §1328, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8439A\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the central\nNew York regional transportation authority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the Central NY Regional Transportation Authority (\"CENTRO\")\nto increase the number of voting board members and makes other clarify-\ning changes to CENTRO's governing statute\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 1328 of the Public Authorities Law to increase\nthe maximum number of members on the CENTRO Board to 13 and clarify that\nthe non -voting member required pursuant to this statute cannot be\ncounted as the additional board member.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nCurrent law stipulates that the CENTRO Board of Directors consist of 12\nmembers, including the chair and one non-voting member.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCentral NY Regional Transportation Authority (\"CENTRO\") is the public\ntransportation provider for the counties of Onondaga, Oswego, Cayuga and\nOneida counties and recently expanded to include Cortland County as its\n5th member. To account for this expansion CENTRO requested this change\nin its enabling legislation. Expanding the board from 12 to 13 members\nprovides CENTRO with the necessary room to allow for representation from\nCortland County.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately, and shall be deemed to be in full force and effect on and\nafter March 31, 2025.\n",
